{# Route registry lives in src/_data/site.json. `nav: false` on the home entry is why it is absent
here: home is reachable via the site title link, exactly as it is today. NOTE: keep angle brackets
out of these Nunjucks comments. Prettier's HTML printer parses tag names inside them as real markup
and mangles the file. YEO-139: home canonicalises to origin + "/", not /index.html. The list items
are wrapped in a ul: they were direct children of nav, which is invalid HTML and costs assistive
technology the list semantics (a screen reader could not say how many items the navigation has).
role="list" is not redundant here - Safari drops the implicit list role from any list carrying
list-style: none, which header nav ul does. The current page is marked aria-current="page". The
whole anchor is duplicated across the branches rather than conditionally emitting a single
attribute: prettier parses this file with its HTML parser, which mangles a Nunjucks tag that sits
inside an element's attribute list. #}
<nav id="site-nav" aria-label="Main">
    <ul role="list">
        {%- for p in site.pages %}{% if p.nav %} {% if p.key == key %}
        <li><a href="{{ p.url }}" aria-current="page">{{ p.label }}</a></li>
        {%- else %}
        <li><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.label }}</a></li>
        {%- endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
</nav>
